invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20_avx2.c
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: chacha20_avx2.c drops the target attribute that turns AVX2 on for
  its own functions, so the kernel compiles only where the whole object is
  built with -mavx2, and an object built that way runs AVX2 in code the
  caller's CH_CPU_AVX2 bit never chose. The script compiles the file for
  x86-64 with no instruction flag and requires the kernel on 256-bit
  registers.

--- old
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((target("avx2"))), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#pragma GCC target("avx2")
#endif
--- new
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((cold)), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#endif
